    "body": "Hi, we recently swtiched to `picocolors` at Astro.\n\nIt works OK. It would be great to switch to ESM, but we can work around it.\n\nThe primary blocker we hit is the use of `process`, which is a global that doesn't exist in all runtimes. For example, `worked` in Cloudflare.\n\nWould you be open to dropping its use? Or having a safer check so it doesn't break in non-Node.js runtimes? ",
